{
 "format": "damap",
 "version": 1,
 "id": "5",
 "name": "Young Ogres and Scout Ogres",
 "file": "Map5_Young_Ogres.xml",
 "rooms": [
  {"id":1,"x":360,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Small, bent satinwoods cling to the rocky slope, their gnarled roots seeking patches of soil.  Tiny purple flowers spread across the ground, thriving and flourishing where the larger and greedier trees barely hang on.  A path levels out to the northwest, following the curve of the outcrop, while to the southwest the way continues on up."],"exits":[{"to":3,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":9,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":2,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cliff"}]},
  {"id":2,"x":380,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A huge rocky outcrop breaks through the thick, loamy soil of the forest as the ground rises and roughens.  Fewer trees grow up here, and those that do cling to what soil they can find are smaller and twisted.  Graceful ferns and lacy grey moss spread across the exposed rocks, softening their harsh outlines."],"exits":[{"to":1,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cliff"},{"to":35,"exit":"climb","move":"climb trail"}]},
  {"id":3,"x":340,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A narrow stony shelf runs along one edge of the rocky outcrop, winding among boulders and gaps and the occasional stunted tree.  The view down to the east is green, a dense tree canopy only a short distance below.  Small grey birds dart back and forth between the trees, quarreling over something."],"exits":[{"to":1,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":4,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":4,"x":300,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A gnarled satinwood tree grows jammed into a shadowy corner, its stunted branches reaching up to the sky.  Ferns rustle in the cold night breeze, punctuated by the call of a distant bird hunting somewhere in the blackness."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":3,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":5,"x":300,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A tangle of trees and shrubs growing in a deep patch of soil forces the path dangerously near the ledge to the east.  The rocky outcrop drops away, giving a view of a vast, dense forest.  Opposite the ledge, the rock rises up high overhead, the grey stone climbable only by spreading lichen and moss."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":4,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":20,"exit":"up","move":"up"}],"aliases":["Ogres"]},
  {"id":6,"x":300,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Millenia of streaming rain have cut vertical grooves into the solid rock of the outcrop.  Looking like the scored bark of some huge grey tree, the grooved stone runs down the rock face into a shadowy hollow."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":7,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":26,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":7,"x":280,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A cool breeze blows past the rocky outcrop and up the slope to the west.  Between the breeze and the perpetual shade here on the north side, it's rather chilly.  The trees don't seem to mind, though, nor do the scrubby bushes that cling to the rocky soil."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":8,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":8,"x":280,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The footing is treacherous here on this particularly steep stretch of winding path.  The trail turns south as it climbs higher, while the lower reaches are down to the east.  Not even bushes grow in this immediate area -- all is steep cliff and featureless rock, with a narrow trail made even more harrowing by gusting winds."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":7,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":9,"x":360,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A few stunted satinwood trees grow in the shallow soil up here on the outcrop.  Yellow-green grass and a few thornbushes fill in the space between the trees.  The bushes occasionally emit a rustling which isn't the product of the stiff breeze -- apparently some sort of small animal makes its home in this area, in whatever cover it can find."],"exits":[{"to":27,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":10,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":1,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":10,"x":340,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A deeper patch of soil is home to a stand of lush bushes with ruffled blue flowers the size of an orange.  Small paw prints lead in and out of the bushes, with an occasional larger paw print showing that predators live here too.  Scruffy looking weeds grow in the rocky soil a distance from the bushes, and very little at all grows up the trail to the west, higher on the outcrop."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":11,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":32,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":11,"x":280,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["This arm of the trail is wide and relatively flat, running between the northern and southern domes of the rocky outcrop.  Tough grass grows all about, and some bushes and an occasional satinwood tree grow here and there about the landscape.  The soil isn't very deep, nor very fertile, and the satinwoods aren't the healthiest specimens, but they persevere, as life always does, and they manage to survive the harsh conditions."],"exits":[{"to":10,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":12,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":12,"x":260,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The northern lobe of the outcrop rises high above, even though this intersection itself is nowhere near ground level.  A spindly looking satinwood tree grows on the slope below and to the east, blocking most of the view in that direction.  No birds flutter in its branches -- the only creatures immediately visible on the tree are some black ants, marching in a line along one of its nearer limbs.  Some large claw marks in the bark suggest that larger animals are about, however."],"exits":[{"to":20,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":11,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":13,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":13,"x":220,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The two mounds of the rocky outcropping cast deep shadows on this narrow gap hardly any light penetrates, even from the stars.  A few ferns and a scrubby bush rustle in the breeze."],"exits":[{"to":12,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":14,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":14,"x":180,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Piles of rubble indicate frequent rockslides on this side of the outcrop.  The loose boulders and rocks and pebbles make footing treacherous.  A narrow trail leads the eye up and to the northeast, toward the ridge crest.  Silhouetted trees whip back and forth in what appear to be strong winds."],"exits":[{"to":13,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":15,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":21,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":15,"x":120,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Coarse vines like grey-green twine cling to what little soil is to be found in hollows and chinks of the rock.  Fireflies swirl and swoop in glowing spirals over the night-darkened vegetation, striving to attract mates with their luminous dance while at the same time avoiding night-hunting predators."],"exits":[{"to":16,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":14,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":24,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":16,"x":120,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The trail winds around this northern lobe of the rocky outcrop, and a smaller path makes its way up to the eastern ridge.  Low bushes with grey-green leaves grow here and there on the slope, finding whatever pockets of soil there may be.  Occasional rustling sounds from the bushes suggest some sort of animal life, although if there are any small creatures here, they stay well hidden."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":15,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":23,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":17,"x":160,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A pile of white bones and a few shreds of rotting hide suggest that something had a good meal not too long ago.  A scrap of what looks like a hare's ear lies to one side, and the bones are about the right size to have been a hare.  Large paw prints cover the ground around the carcass, but they're too overlapped to show where the predator went."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":16,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":18,"x":220,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The view to the northwest is grand at this elevation, with the landscape spread out like a patchwork quilt.  An eagle soars in the distance, keeping a sharp eye out for prey on the distant ground.  Closer in, the path curves east and west around the boundary of the rocky outcrop.  Sea level is far below, and most of the surfaces within immediate reach are vertical."],"exits":[{"to":19,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":17,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":8,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":19,"x":260,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Stringy creepers spread out across the rock like a fisherman's net spread to dry.  Ragged bell-shaped blossoms in a pale yellow decorate the vines, their petals glowing in the starlight.  Fireflies swirl and dance above the flowers, leaving glowing afterimages in the blackness.  Down in the dry dirt among the creepers is a large paw print, suggesting that creatures larger than fireflies do frequent this place."],"exits":[{"to":20,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":18,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":25,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":20,"x":260,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The path runs straight north and south here, scoured clean of dirt by the gusting wind.  A narrower trail, out of the wind but rough with loose stones, winds its way down the slope to the east.  Farther east and much closer to the ground, a deep green forest spreads across the land.  Farther yet, beyond the forest, are the regular, colored patches that mark croplands.  A tiny village is barely discernable as an irregular blotch in the rectangular blocks of fieldland."],"exits":[{"to":19,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":12,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":5,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":21,"x":180,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Ridge","descriptions":["An intrepid bird has made a nest high up in one of the stunted trees.  The nest is a marvel of engineering, clinging to the branches with grass and vines and mud-plaster.  That it's survived the steady, strong winds way up here speaks well of the stubborn bird who built it."],"exits":[{"to":22,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":14,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":22,"x":180,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Ridge","descriptions":["Wind-blown grit has sculpted the stone into fanciful shapes, scouring out the softer stone and leaving the harder layers ridged and twisted.  One spire looks rather like a chess piece, from the right angle."],"exits":[{"to":21,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":23,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":23,"x":160,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Ridge","descriptions":["The winds whip through the branches of the short, stunted trees up here on the ridge line.  It's uncomfortably cold, and eyes watering from the wind can't even properly appreciate the view.  Footing is good, since the wind has blown away loose stones and soil, leaving only what is well-anchored."],"exits":[{"to":22,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":16,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":24,"x":120,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Slope","descriptions":["The slope on this side of the outcrop is just barely navigable, about down to here.  The drop-off farther to the west is vertical, and the thought of climbing down it is unpleasant.  The view is spectacular, however, and the western lands spread out from one horizon to the other are awe-inspiring in their beauty and variety."],"exits":[{"to":15,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":25,"x":240,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Notch","descriptions":["This narrow notch between two huge rocks is home to nothing more complex than some yellowish grass and a bit of lacy grey moss that blends nearly invisibly into the stone.  Little light penetrates here, and the atmosphere is bare and gloomy.  The only positive note about this place is that the same rocks which shade it also block the winds."],"exits":[{"to":19,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":26,"x":280,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Shaded Hollow","descriptions":["Lush green ferns line this hollow in the rock.  The soil is thicker here, with the dry bed of a tiny stream, probably carved by flowing rain water, running down from above and disappearing into a dry, cracked basin.  Towering stone rises high overhead in every direction, making this hollow uncomfortably cool even though it's protected from the wind."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":27,"x":360,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The view to the east, of lush, green forest and a glistening brook, is a sharp contrast to the harsher landscape in the immediate area.  The deep, fertile soil of the forest is only a wish up here, where the ground is rocky and dry, with little loam in it.  Plants are smaller, tougher, and less colorful than down on the flatlands."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":28,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":28,"x":320,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The trail west leads up, higher onto the outcrop.  The breeze down here is cool and strong, but the branches of trees further up whip back and forth as though possessed by demons.  Just looking up at it makes one feel cold.  A smaller trail leading down to the southwest looks treacherous, but at least it doesn't look quite so chilly down there."],"exits":[{"to":27,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":30,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":29,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":29,"x":320,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Crumbly Ledge","descriptions":["This ledge feels like it's about to fall off the rock face at any time.  Tough grass grows in the soil captured by cracks in the rock, and the roots of the plants pry, very slowly, at the stone, forcing it farther and farther apart.  Some day it'll give, and the ledge, and anything -- or any one -- on it will plunge down onto the flatlands below."],"exits":[{"to":28,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":30,"x":320,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The wind up here finds every gap and chink in clothing, armor, and anything else one might wrap up in.  The plant life, at least, doesn't seem to mind and other plants grow low to the ground.  No extravagant explosions of leaf or flower here -- everything is small, sturdy, and functional."],"exits":[{"to":31,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":28,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":31,"x":320,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A wide spot in the trail invites a rest, and a clear view to the east invites a long, admiring look.  A verdant forest spreads out immediately below the rocky outcrop, stitched with the narrow thread of a glittering brook across its middle.  Beyond the forest lies cropland, planted in greens and browns and beiges, laid out like a game board.  A small village lies far to the east, nestled among the fields and orchards."],"exits":[{"to":30,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":32,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":32,"x":300,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A patch of white puffy flowers spreads out across the ground, their dark green tendrils seeking out soil and water.  One mound of flowers looks like it's been chewed on, and some small paw prints in the dirt confirm the impression."],"exits":[{"to":31,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":33,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":10,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":33,"x":280,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A crooked intersection in the trail splits the way into three branches.  A flat path runs east, and seems to be the easiest way to go.  A narrower trail winds up the side of the outcrop to the south, while a gap between a couple of rocks to the southwest leads down into shadow.  The ground here is scoured clean of soil by the winds, and there are no tracks to indicate which path might be the more heavily travelled."],"exits":[{"to":32,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":34,"exit":"down","move":"down"},{"to":36,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rockface"}]},
  {"id":34,"x":280,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Hollow","descriptions":["This small hollow in the stone of the outcrop is surprisingly pleasant.  Dry rivulets in the ground suggest that rainwater carries loose dirt from higher on the mound and deposits it here, creating an oasis of both soil and water.  A variety of plants grow in this place -- little yellow bell-shaped flowers, puffy white ones, and tiny purple ones that grow scattered amongst all the others.  A vine with shiny leaves climbs up the walls, softening the otherwise harsh contours of the stone."],"exits":[{"to":33,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":35,"x":400,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Dense Forest","descriptions":["Stray beams of sunlight filter down through the dense, leafy trees, turning the floating dust motes into dancing fairies.  The ground rises to the west, and turns rockier, the trees thinning out a bit in the less fertile soil.","Hooting calls and low hums and clicks signal the presence of woodland life, even though none of it is visible in the darkness.  The dense, leafy trees cast deep shadows on the forest floor, dark patches that could be hiding almost anything.  The land rises slightly to the west, and there seem to be more rocks in the soil in that direction."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":2,"exit":"climb","move":"climb trail"}],"linksTo":"Map4_Crossing_WestGate.xml"},
  {"id":36,"x":220,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The steep trail takes a turn here, curving from the north to the southwest as it climbs.  Loose rock and pebbles make the footing uncertain, requiring complete concentration.  An occasional howling cry, blasting through the cold air, makes concentration difficult, however."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":33,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rockface"}]},
  {"id":37,"x":220,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The trail winds around a slab of grey rock that thrusts into the air like a watchtower.  The winds are sharp this high up, slicing like frozen knives into every chink and opening in clothing or armor.  The only plants are low-growing, strongly rooted, or both. "],"exits":[{"to":38,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":39,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":36,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":38,"x":240,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Looking down from the crest of the rocky outcrop, the change of terrain between the rocks and the forest is obvious.  The dominant color on this side is grey -- grey rocks and grey-green foliage, spotted with occasional patches of dusty color where ever a plant has decided to put up flowers.  On the forest side the dominant color is a rich green, where lush trees and grass and ferns blend with larger and more colorful flowers."],"exits":[{"to":42,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":37,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":39,"x":220,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A single gnarled satinwood stands here, bent and twisted by the wind until it resembles nothing so much as a gnarled hand growing out of the rocky soil, all its fingers yearning toward the west.  A few low, mossy plants cling to its roots, sending up tiny purple flowers a bare fingerwidth above the ground."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":40,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":40,"x":240,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Tiny purple flowers cover the rocky summit.  Their mossy green foliage grows low to the ground, their roots digging in deep in search of both water and anchorage.  A few patches of the mossy plants look crushed or nibbled, but no loose soil is allowed to collect here, and there are no tracks to indicate what might have been browsing."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":39,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":41,"x":280,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Strong winds howl through the blackness of the night, finding unimagined gaps in clothing and armor.  Spread to the east is only more blackness, but lit by a few lights, here and there.  One is relatively close, east and a bit south, a small flicker indicating a band or perhaps a small village.  Slightly larger is the flickering glow from farther east, about halfway from here to the horizon.  And on the horizon itself is a spot that lights up a patch of land as broad as an outstretched hand. "],"exits":[{"to":42,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":40,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":42,"x":280,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A patch of low thornbushes crowns the rock at the base of a taller spire.  Sheltered somewhat from the wind, the bushes have managed to spread out and grow to about waist high.  Despite the lack of wind on this side of the spire, however, the bushes sway and rustle -- apparently something else has also taken advantage of the calmer air and the shelter of the foliage."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":38,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]}
 ],
 "labels": [
  {"text":"Young Ogres, Scout Ogres","x":90,"y":10,"z":0},
  {"text":"Blood Wolf","x":100,"y":50,"z":0},
  {"text":"Westgate Hunting Area","x":390,"y":190,"z":0}
 ]
}
